IIRC, CONFIG_ISA sufficed in the earlier version, but this might have
been an incident that ISAPNP was (automatically) turned on.

In 2.6.17, even CONFIG_ISA is removed from the dependency of vxpocket
driver.  I've not checked whether really the driver works really
without CONFIG_ISA and CONFIG_ISAPNP.

If ISAPNP is still required in 2.6.17, you should report it to kernel
bugzilla or LKML.  I think the pcmcia controller side should have a
proper dependency on ISA or ISAPNP.


